  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Mod-φ convergence, II: Estimates on the speed of convergence — In this paper, we give estimates for the speed of convergence towards a limiting stable law in the recently introduced setting of mod-φ\n\n**Mod-φ convergence, II: Estimates on the speed of convergence**\n\n*Valentin Féray, Pierre-Loïc Méliot, and Ashkan Nikeghbali*\n\n53 pp, 27 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this paper, we give estimates for the speed of convergence towards a limiting stable law in the recently introduced setting of mod-φ convergence. Namely, we deﬁne a notion of zone of control, closely related to mod-φ convergence, and we prove estimates of Berry–Esseen type under this hypothesis. Applications include: • the winding number of a planar Brownian motion; • classical approximations of stable laws by compound Poisson laws; • examples stemming from determinantal point processes (characteristic polynomials of random matri- ces and zeroes of random analytic functions); • sums of variables with an underlying dependency graph (for which we recover a result of Rinott, obtained by Stein’s method); • the magnetization in the d-dimensional Ising model; • and functionals of Markov chains.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Mod-$\\phi$ convergence; 1.2 Results and outline of the paper; 1.3 Stable distributions and mod-stable conver; 2 Speed of convergence estimates; 2.1 The notion of zone of control; 2.2 Spaces of test functions; 2.3 Estimates for test functions; 2.4 Smoothing techniques; 2.5 Bounds on the Kolmogorov distance; 3 Examples with an explicit Fourier transform; 3.1 Sums of independent random variables; 3.2 Winding number of a planar Brownian motion; 3.3 Approximation of a stable law by compound ; 3.4 Convergence of Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process; 3.5 Logarithms of characteristic polynomials o; 4 Cumulants and dependency graphs",
